      "summaries": {
        "en": "Tolaria is a desktop app that helps you manage and organize markdown knowledge bases, solving the problem of scattered notes and documents. It provides a clean interface for browsing, editing, and linking markdown files, with features like full-text search and graph visualization to reveal connections between notes. You can use it to build a personal wiki, a project documentation hub, or a research notebook, making it easy to maintain and explore your knowledge over time.",
        "zh": "Tolaria 是一款桌面应用，用于管理和组织 Markdown 知识库，解决笔记和文档分散的问题。它提供简洁的界面来浏览、编辑和链接 Markdown 文件，支持全文搜索和图形可视化，帮助发现笔记之间的关联。你可以用它搭建个人维基、项目文档中心或研究笔记，轻松维护和探索知识。其核心优势在于专注于本地 Markdown 文件，无需复杂配置，即可实现知识的结构化与互联。",
        "es": "Tolaria is a desktop app that helps you manage and organize markdown knowledge bases, solving the problem of scattered notes and documents. It provides a clean interface for browsing, editing, and linking markdown files, with features like full-text search and graph visualization to reveal connections between notes. You can use it to build a personal wiki, a project documentation hub, or a research notebook, making it easy to maintain and explore your knowledge over time.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "tolaria gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Tolaria is a desktop app that helps you manage and organize markdown knowledge bases, solving the problem of scattered notes and documents. It provides a clean interface for browsing, editing, and linking markdown files, with features like full-text search and graph visualization to reveal connections between notes. You can use it to build a personal wiki, a project documentation hub, or a research notebook, making it easy to maintain and explore your knowledge over time.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/refactoringhq/tolaria for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
