      "summaries": {
        "en": "pg_durable is a PostgreSQL extension that brings durable execution directly into the database, enabling reliable, long-running workflows without external orchestrators. It leverages PostgreSQL's transactional guarantees to ensure each step of a workflow is persisted and recoverable, even after crashes. Developers can use it to build fault-tolerant AI pipelines, data processing chains, or business workflows entirely within SQL, simplifying infrastructure and reducing operational complexity.",
        "zh": "pg_durable 是一个 PostgreSQL 扩展，将持久化执行能力嵌入数据库内部，使开发者无需外部编排系统即可构建可靠的长时工作流。其核心设计利用 PostgreSQL 的事务机制，确保工作流每一步被持久化记录，崩溃后可从断点恢复。这启示我们：数据库不仅是存储层，也可成为可靠执行引擎。实际应用中，可用于构建容错 AI 推理流水线、多步骤数据处理或复杂业务流程，所有逻辑在 SQL 中定义，简化技术栈。对已使用 PostgreSQL 的团队，pg_durable 提供低心智负担的工作流持久化方案，尤其适合强一致性场景。",
        "es": "pg_durable is a PostgreSQL extension that brings durable execution directly into the database, enabling reliable, long-running workflows without external orchestrators. It leverages PostgreSQL's transactional guarantees to ensure each step of a workflow is persisted and recoverable, even after crashes. Developers can use it to build fault-tolerant AI pipelines, data processing chains, or business workflows entirely within SQL, simplifying infrastructure and reducing operational complexity.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "pg_durable stands out for ai-pipelines, ai-workflows, and durable-execution in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "pg_durable is a PostgreSQL extension that brings durable execution directly into the database, enabling reliable, long-running workflows without external orchestrators. It leverages PostgreSQL's transactional guarantees to ensure each step of a workflow is persisted and recoverable, even after crashes. Developers can use it to build fault-tolerant AI pipelines, data processing chains, or business workflows entirely within SQL, simplifying infrastructure and reducing operational complexity.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/microsoft/pg_durable for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
